ied the\n  workspace; use `report_blocked` only once you've established (via tool calls) that\n  the task can't be done. Both terminate the trial — choose carefully.\n\n\n\nYou are a helpful assistant attempting to submit the best possible answer. You have several tools available to help with finding the answer. You will see the result of tool calls right after sending the message. If you need to perform multiple actions, you can always send more messages with additional tool calls. Do some reasoning before your actions, describing what tool calls you are going to use and how they fit into your plan.\n"},{"role":"user","content":"Got a token already (tk_tw_8841) and the existing Metro draft alert is alrt-9f3a. I'm trying to publish it but the call keeps 422'ing on me. Here's exactly what I'm sending:\n\n<request>\nPOST {{base_url}}/v3/alerts\nheaders: Authorization: Bearer tk_tw_8841\nbody: {\"snapshot_id\": \"snap-7c2e-2201\", \"stop_id\": \"stop-union-91\", \"severity\": \"critical\", \"headline\": \"Union Station disruption\"}\n</request>\nError: 422 {\"error\": \"invalid_enum\", \"field\": \"severity\", \"allowed\": [\"info\",\"minor\",\"major\",\"severe\"]}\n\nRepair the payload so it's a structurally valid alert create against snap-7c2e-2201's disrupted stop at the highest non-emergency severity, then carry it through to a confirmed published state on the Metro feed and give me the publish_ref the live digest reports.\n\nWhen you have finished, report your final answer as a single JSON object inside a ```json code block, with exactly these field(s): `publish_ref`. Use the exact field name(s) shown, and put each requested value as that field's value."},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":""}],"tool_calls":[{"id":"toolu_01XEdEiUJb3dfCEsXWoiL4Yg","name":"search","arguments":{"query":"alerts"}},{"id":"toolu_014iM3z8A6r4sipvyjHNvWWk","name":"search","arguments":{"query":"snap-7c2e-2201"}},{"id":"toolu_019HZMJqJLcXbLXESeJAzuxf","name":"sea